infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title B-tree vs GIN: the per-write tax
  desc Same insert, different index type — GIN can cost up to 4x the per-row write overhead of a B-tree
  compares
    - label B-tree (one ordered value per row)
      children
        - label 5-50 us per write
          desc One sorted entry updated per indexed column
        - label ~10-30% of table size
          desc A single key per row on disk
        - label HOT can skip it
          desc If no indexed column changed and the page has space, the index write is eliminated
    - label GIN on high-write JSONB
      children
        - label 50-200 us per row
          desc Every key in the document touches a separate posting list
        - label 2-5x the indexed data
          desc One entry per key, array element, or lexeme
        - label fastupdate defers it
          desc Buffer GIN maintenance to a background flush, or narrow to an expression index on a hot field
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
